# Displays for watching RTAB-Map build the map.
#
# RViz rewrites this file wholesale whenever you save from the GUI, and its
# writer drops comments. If this block is missing, that is what happened; the
# displays themselves survive. Put it back rather than assuming it was removed
# on purpose.
#
# Topic names carry no /rtabmap prefix. RTAB-Map's own documentation writes
# /rtabmap/cloud_map because its upstream launch files put the node in an
# 'rtabmap' namespace; rtabmap.launch.py sets none, so that /map lands where
# Nav2 looks for it. /rtabmap/anything does not exist here.
#
# What each cloud is, since they are easy to confuse:
#   Cloud Map          /cloud_map, occupancy cells as points. Flat by
#                      construction, because Grid/3D is false so every cell
#                      sits at one height. This is what Nav2 is handed.
#   Dense Cloud Map    /dense_map/cloud_map, the real 3D map. Needs
#                      dense_map:=true, which starts map_assembler; empty
#                      without it.
#   Lidar              /lidar/points with a 60 s decay, the rawest and densest
#                      view. Those points are placed by the TF at arrival and
#                      do not move on loop closure, so trust Dense Cloud Map
#                      for map geometry.
#
# Two displays ship disabled on purpose: Camera, because the image panel
# crowds the 3D view, and Estimated Odometry, because nothing publishes
# /rtabmap/odom under the default odom_source:=ground_truth, where
# gt_odom_tf.py broadcasts a transform and no Odometry message at all.
Panels:
  - Class: rviz_common/Displays
    Help Height: 138
    Name: Displays
    Property Tree Widget:
      Expanded:
        - /Lidar (60 s trail)1
        - /Camera1
      Splitter Ratio: 0.5
    Tree Height: 810
